I now have comprehensive findings from all research. Let me synthesize my review.

**Key findings from independent verification:**
- All references confirmed real and accurately described
- Robometer confirmed: provides dense frame-level rewards, LIBERO checkpoint available, BUT not tested on RoboMimic
- Robometer + IQL is already combined by Robometer authors, but only for offline RL training — NOT for V/A-based curation (ADTS's novelty is genuine here)
- CoRL 2026 deadlines confirmed (abstract May 26, paper May 29) — but idea targets ICLR 2027, not CoRL 2026
- Three close competitors missed: AWR family (advantage-weighted training), VACO (ICLR 2025, value-aligned behavior cloning), IDRL (iterative transition filtering)
- No exact prior art found for the 2D V×A curation scoring — the specific combination appears novel

